,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"**Migrated issue, originally created by Alana Pradhan**\n\nI think this bug is an extension of https://bitbucket.org/zzzeek/sqlalchemy/issues/3969/negation-of-labeled-element\n\nI hit this bug in 1.2.10 when I add `.self_group()` to the or_ expression:\n\n\n```\nfrom sqlalchemy import *\nfrom sqlalchemy.dialects import sqlite\nexpr = or_(column('x') == 1, column('y') == 2).self_group()\n\nbug = not_(expr.label('foo'))\n\n\n\nprint(bug.compile())\nprint(bug.compile(dialect=sqlite.dialect()))\n\n```\n\n```\nNOT (x = :x_1 OR y = :y_1)\n(x = ? OR y = ?) = 0\n```\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4320/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4320/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]